WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.980
The 2001 comedy Zoolander features an array
of Hollywood celebs in its cast.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.320
Besides core stars like Ben Stiller, Owen
Wilson, and Will Ferrell, the movie boasts

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.769
appearances by actors like Judah Friedlander,
Alexander Skarsgård, and Andy Dick, among

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:15.300
many other famous faces.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:19.820
But chances are you may have missed one major
celebrity who was hiding in plain sight.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:25.000
After Stiller's model character Derek Zoolander
is captured by villain Mugatu's evil team,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:30.260
henchman Katinka, played by real-life supermodel
Milla Jovovich, signals to a DJ to start the

00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:31.640
brainwashing process.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.870
The performer, donning dreadlocks, a stub
of a beard on his chin, and a nasty-looking

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:40.690
facial scar, puts down a record and starts
playing a remix of "Relax" by the popular

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.660
'80s band Frankie Goes To Hollywood.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:47.800
The gold-toothed baddie also memorably fights
Wilson's Hansel in a breakdancing battle,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:48.940
because, why not?

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:52.800
But just who was the man portraying the devious
disc jockey?

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.100
None other than actor Justin Theroux!

00:00:55.220 --> 00:01:00.480
Yep, the guy who starred in the HBO drama
The Leftovers played the character "Evil DJ."

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.380
And apparently those breakdancing moves were
all his.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:06.700
Theroux told TV host Conan O'Brien in September
2014:

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:12.380
"Yes, I learned when I was around, I don't
know, 12 or 13, somewhere in there, how to

00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:13.390
breakdance…

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:15.950
And I had a little crew that we used to roll
around Washington, D.C."

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.560
Stiller apparently decided to make use of
Theroux's skills for Zoolander after seeing

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:22.420
him breakdance at his wedding to actress Christine
Taylor.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:27.060
Theroux later reprised the character of Evil
DJ for the comedy's 2016 sequel, Zoolander

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:31.469
2, the screenplay for which he also helped
write with Stiller, Nicholas Stoller, and

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:32.080
John Hamburg.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:36.740
"Relax."

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.140
He also dressed as Evil DJ on the red carpet
for the premiere of the second film, posing

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:46.429
for cameras in a white New York Yankees hoodie
and gold sneakers, as reported by Hello!

00:01:46.429 --> 00:01:47.080
Magazine.

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:48.880
"How's the family reunion going?"

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:50.280
"Great.

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.780
I'd like to check him out for a few hours,
if that's okay."

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:55.520
"Sure, long as he's back by sundown."

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:00.300
Regarding working on Zoolander 2 with Stiller,
Theroux told Business Insider in 2016:

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.299
"I think we were all like, let's not try to
beat the first one, let's not think about

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:04.920
it like that.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:08.979
Let's think about where the characters would
be historically 10 years later and see if

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.920
there's a funny idea of them being aged out."

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:11.860
He continued:

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.260
"We basically decided to run right at the
fact that, yeah, they are older, instead of

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.370
trying to pick up the movie one day after
or one week later.

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:23.320
We thought it would be funny if they were
washed up and had to come back into the industry."

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:27.500
His role in Zoolander and Zoolander 2 aside,
Theroux has made a name for himself on the

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:32.260
small and big screens with projects like Maniac,
The Girl on the Train, and On the Basis of

00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:32.760
Sex.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.700
Not only an actor, he's also a writer, lending
his talents to the 2008 comedy Tropic Thunder

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:40.060
and the 2010 Marvel movie Iron Man 2.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:45.220
Despite his long list of film and TV gigs,
fans of celebrity news may know him best for

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.360
his relationship with movie star and Friends
alum Jennifer Aniston.

00:02:48.849 --> 00:02:52.720
As noted by Cosmopolitan magazine, Theroux
and Aniston were first thought to have gotten

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:56.660
together in May 2011, and, before long, the
two reportedly moved in together.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:03:01.170
By August 2012, Theroux had proposed to his
lady love, and the celebrity couple tied the

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.560
knot in August 2015.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:06.120
Unfortunately, Theroux and Aniston wouldn't
remain together.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:11.000
On Feb. 15, 2018, they announced that they
had separated, saying, in a joint statement

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.400
reported by Us Weekly:

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.519
"We are two best friends who have decided
to part ways as a couple, but look forward

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:18.470
to continuing our cherished friendship."

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.240
But don't feel too bad for Theroux.

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:23.780
He appears to be doing well following the
"heartbreaking" breakup, and he has at least

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.820
one major acting gig on the horizon.

00:03:26.049 --> 00:03:30.519
In July 2018, Collider announced that Theroux
would be voicing the character of Tramp in

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:32.440
Disney's remake of Lady and the Tramp.

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:33.680
As for Lady?

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.540
She'll reportedly be voiced by Thor: Ragnarok's
Tessa Thompson.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.180
Who would have guessed that Evil DJ would
wind up working for the House of Mouse?

